{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Column definitions can contain Lit template results, directives, nodes, primitive values, iterables, or renderer functions for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"header"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cell"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"footer"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aggregatedCell"},{"type":"text","value":". Use the adapter's rendering utilities inside Lit templates so those values receive their table context."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"flexrender-vs-flexrender","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FlexRender"},{"type":"text","value":" vs "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"flexRender"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In Lit, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FlexRender"},{"type":"text","value":" is a convenience function rather than a custom element. Pass exactly one "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cell"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"header"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"footer"},{"type":"text","value":" object and interpolate the result:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"html`\n  <thead>\n    ${table.getHeaderGroups().map(\n      (headerGroup) => html`\n        <tr>\n          ${headerGroup.headers.map(\n            (header) => html`\n              <th>${header.isPlaceholder ? null : FlexRender({ header })}</th>\n            `,\n          )}\n        </tr>\n      `,\n    )}\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    ${table.getRowModel().rows.map(\n      (row) => html`\n        <tr>\n          ${row\n            .getVisibleCells()\n            .map((cell) => html`<td>${FlexRender({ cell })}</td>`)}\n        </tr>\n      `,\n    )}\n  </tbody>\n`","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Import it from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/lit-table"},{"type":"text","value":". Tables returned by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TableController"},{"type":"text","value":" also expose it as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.FlexRender"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For cells, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FlexRender"},{"type":"text","value":" selects "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aggregatedCell"},{"type":"text","value":" for aggregated rows, falls back to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cell"},{"type":"text","value":", and returns "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"null"},{"type":"text","value":" for grouping placeholders. Pass footer-group "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Header"},{"type":"text","value":" objects as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FlexRender({ footer: header })"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"flexRender"},{"type":"text","value":" is the lower-level function for a renderable value and context:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"flexRender(cell.column.columnDef.cell, cell.getContext())","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"It calls function renderers and passes every other "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"LitRenderable"},{"type":"text","value":" through unchanged. It does not choose the appropriate grouped-cell renderer or suppress placeholders, so prefer "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FlexRender"},{"type":"text","value":" for ordinary table markup."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Placeholder headers remain the template's layout decision. Check "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"header.isPlaceholder"},{"type":"text","value":" unless the placeholder intentionally provides content for a spanning header."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"flexrender-vs-flexrender","text":"FlexRender vs flexRender","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nColumn definitions can contain Lit template results, directives, nodes, primitive values, iterables, or renderer functions for `header`, `cell`, `footer`, and `aggregatedCell`. Use the adapter's rendering utilities inside Lit templates so those values receive their table context.\n\n## `FlexRender` vs `flexRender`\n\nIn Lit, `FlexRender` is a convenience function rather than a custom element. Pass exactly one `cell`, `header`, or `footer` object and interpolate the result:\n\n```ts\nhtml`\n  <thead>\n    ${table.getHeaderGroups().map(\n      (headerGroup) => html`\n        <tr>\n          ${headerGroup.headers.map(\n            (header) => html`\n              <th>${header.isPlaceholder ? null : FlexRender({ header })}</th>\n            `,\n          )}\n        </tr>\n      `,\n    )}\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    ${table.getRowModel().rows.map(\n      (row) => html`\n        <tr>\n          ${row\n            .getVisibleCells()\n            .map((cell) => html`<td>${FlexRender({ cell })}</td>`)}\n        </tr>\n      `,\n    )}\n  </tbody>\n`\n```\n\nImport it from `@tanstack/lit-table`. Tables returned by `TableController` also expose it as `table.FlexRender`.\n\nFor cells, `FlexRender` selects `aggregatedCell` for aggregated rows, falls back to `cell`, and returns `null` for grouping placeholders. Pass footer-group `Header` objects as `FlexRender({ footer: header })`.\n\n`flexRender` is the lower-level function for a renderable value and context:\n\n```ts\nflexRender(cell.column.columnDef.cell, cell.getContext())\n```\n\nIt calls function renderers and passes every other `LitRenderable` through unchanged. It does not choose the appropriate grouped-cell renderer or suppress placeholders, so prefer `FlexRender` for ordinary table markup.\n\nPlaceholder headers remain the template's layout decision. Check `header.isPlaceholder` unless the placeholder intentionally provides content for a spanning header.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: FlexRender (Lit) Guide\n---\n\nColumn definitions can contain Lit template results, directives, nodes, primitive values, iterables, or renderer functions for `header`, `cell`, `footer`, and `aggregatedCell`. Use the adapter's rendering utilities inside Lit templates so those values receive their table context.\n\n## `FlexRender` vs `flexRender`\n\nIn Lit, `FlexRender` is a convenience function rather than a custom element. Pass exactly one `cell`, `header`, or `footer` object and interpolate the result:\n\n```ts\nhtml`\n  <thead>\n    ${table.getHeaderGroups().map(\n      (headerGroup) => html`\n        <tr>\n          ${headerGroup.headers.map(\n            (header) => html`\n              <th>${header.isPlaceholder ? null : FlexRender({ header })}</th>\n            `,\n          )}\n        </tr>\n      `,\n    )}\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    ${table.getRowModel().rows.map(\n      (row) => html`\n        <tr>\n          ${row\n            .getVisibleCells()\n            .map((cell) => html`<td>${FlexRender({ cell })}</td>`)}\n        </tr>\n      `,\n    )}\n  </tbody>\n`\n```\n\nImport it from `@tanstack/lit-table`. Tables returned by `TableController` also expose it as `table.FlexRender`.\n\nFor cells, `FlexRender` selects `aggregatedCell` for aggregated rows, falls back to `cell`, and returns `null` for grouping placeholders. Pass footer-group `Header` objects as `FlexRender({ footer: header })`.\n\n`flexRender` is the lower-level function for a renderable value and context:\n\n```ts\nflexRender(cell.column.columnDef.cell, cell.getContext())\n```\n\nIt calls function renderers and passes every other `LitRenderable` through unchanged. It does not choose the appropriate grouped-cell renderer or suppress placeholders, so prefer `FlexRender` for ordinary table markup.\n\nPlaceholder headers remain the template's layout decision. Check `header.isPlaceholder` unless the placeholder intentionally provides content for a spanning header.\n"}
